    description: "WHAT (as reported)\nElectron (electron-react-boilerplate, the common starting template): the IPC linker read 19 files and produced 0 links, reporting candidates_unresolved. The preload script is a pass-through wrapper that takes the channel as a parameter (sendMessage(channel) calling ipcRenderer.send(channel)), so the sender sendMessage('ipc-example') at index.tsx line 12 is never tied to ipcMain.on('ipc-example'). A generic event-name matcher did group the main-process handler and the page's once('ipc-example') listener under one channel. A reverse slice from the handler finds 1 edge. ADR-0054 names the cause (a channel that is not a string literal is skipped) and added the candidates_unresolved label; this item asks for the link.\n\nNOT CHECKED\nThe unreleased work on Electron preload scripts (changelog: \"Electron IPC handlers and preload scripts\") against this template. Related, distinct: WI-pisur (an IPC call in a comment), WI-bokip (preload path into build output).\n\nREPORTED, NOT RE-RUN. Source: an outside reviewer who tried hypergumbo 10.0.0 from PyPI on 2026-11-24 (transcript pasted by the owner in session). Nothing in this item was run on dev by the filing agent unless a line says so; the reviewer's fixtures are not on this machine. FIRST STEP: reproduce on current dev with a fixture, and check the unreleased changelog, before building anything. Filed at the owner's request (\"file them all now\")."  # 8d01
